      "worked_solution": "Since we need to multiply $\\dfrac{\\color{red}1}{5}$ by $\\color{blue}3$, we repeat the fraction model $\\color{blue}3$ times, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129500/assets/fe41721739d82df825d2a7e28bc19590fbc784354a58aa74137aceda0e6be202.png)\n\n \n\nThere are ${\\color{blue}3} \\times {\\color{red}1} = 3$ shaded pieces in total. Therefore, \n\n$$\n3 \\times \\dfrac{1}{5} = \\dfrac{3}{5}.\n$$",
